            <title>[LU-20478] sanityn: test_109: "VFS: Busy inodes after unmount" and "Objects remaining in lustre_inode_cache" at rmmod (mount-instance race)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20478</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Hiroshi Nishida &amp;lt;hnishida@thelustrecollective.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5ab41deb-fb0a-43ea-81f3-5c8a597c2936" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/5ab41deb-fb0a-43ea-81f3-5c8a597c2936&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127505" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127505&lt;/a&gt; - 4.18.0-553.137.1.el8_10.x86_64&lt;br/&gt;
servers: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127505" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/127505&lt;/a&gt; - 4.18.0-553.137.1.el8_10_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The test injects cfs_fail_race id 1417 in ll_fill_super(); one racing mount aborted mid-fill (rc=4998), leaving live inodes on the superblock → busy inodes at umount → lustre_inode_cache slab objects remaining when the next module reload hit rmmod (lustre_exit → kmem_cache_destroy). Same race family as &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14110" title="Race during several client mount instances (--&amp;gt; rmmod lustre hang)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14110"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14110&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;/&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-14547" title="santyn/109 fails on a local setup" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-14547"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-14547&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (both Fixed), distinct end symptom, so filed as a recurrence.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
